    "healthcare": "For a 24-bed medical‑surgical unit with 32 nurses working three shifts, design an observation schedule that allocates 40 hand‑hygiene observations per month proportionally across shifts. Specify the exact number of observations each shift should receive and how two trained auditors should distribute their time to cover those observations. For each observation, list all data points that must be recorded for it to be considered valid under WHO's Five Moments framework (including patient identifier, nurse ID, shift/time, moment type, hand‑hygiene action performed or omitted, product used, and any relevant contextual notes). Finally, outline a clear method for compiling these observations into a monthly report that can be presented to the unit’s leadership, including key metrics, visualizations, and actionable insights."
